# A call on a value of a known class runs what that class runs: `feed.read()` on a `Feed(Trimmed, Logged)` runs
# `Trimmed.read` on the feed, whose `super().read()` runs `Logged.read`, the next `read` along the feed's order, and
# nothing else. `Logged.read` writes the log whenever it runs, so what the route then reads of the log is what its own
# step wrote: it reads it back, and the log stands between the step that writes it and the route that reads and uses it.
# On a value of any class a trimmed source may be, `super().read()` may run `Source.read` instead, which writes no log;
# that is no run of this route.

route feeds.run
step run/Feed()
step run/Feed.read                                                   # `feed.read()`, Trimmed.read on the feed
step run/Feed.read/Logged.read                                       # `super().read()` on a feed
step run/Feed.read/Logged.read/Source.read                           # Logged's `super().read()` on the feed

line entry > run call
line run/Feed() > Feed·feed@run/Feed() value
line Feed·feed@run/Feed() > run/Feed.read/Logged.read/Source.read value   # the feed each `read` runs on, handed down by `super()`
line run/Feed.read/Logged.read > File(data/log.txt) own
line File(data/news.txt) > run/Feed.read/Logged.read/Source.read own
line run/Feed.read/Logged.read/Source.read > run/Feed.read/Logged.read back
line run/Feed.read/Logged.read > run/Feed.read back
line run/Feed.read > run back                                        # `news`
line File(data/log.txt) > run own                                    # `LOG.read_text()`, what Logged.read wrote
line run > File(data/log.txt) own

home Feed·feed@run/Feed() run

side entry left
side File(data/news.txt) left
side File(data/log.txt) between
